# The full-suite lock (cmd-start-review): a runtime artifact, never committed.
meta/kanban/.full-suite.lock

# The guards' sandbox manifest (tests/test_suite_profile.py): written into a
# throwaway tree so the copy judges the parent's TRACKED file set rather than
# whatever is on that disk. A stray copy at the repository root is host state
# and is ignored there by _files_under_guard (CARD-239, F-306); this line is
# the other half of that decision.
.card238-tracked

# forge:review step 5a writes its impact set here. Never tracked (0 files on main,
# measured 2026-11-03), and it must stay that way: an untracked-but-unignored
# artefact inflates a Touches re-derivation (CARD-332 cycle 2 measured 16 vs 15)
# and is one loose pathspec away from the committed-artefact harm CARD-335 owns.
meta/impact/

# CARD-335: the measurement artefacts that feed the architecture validator's
# check-ref resolver. That resolver is a TEXT search over TRACKED, non-Markdown
# files (`git grep -lw <ref> -- . :(exclude)meta/architecture :(exclude)*.md`),
# so a tracked artefact that merely SPELLS a ref name makes a dead ref read as
# alive and silently retires its warning. Measured on this tree with the
# resolver's own instrument (tests/test_check_ref_resolution.py): 10 declared
# refs are kept alive by nothing but these three populations.
#
# Ignoring them does not untrack the ones already in the index (that is an
# owner decision, and `kanban done` step 2d/INV-023 forbids a card branch from
# committing under meta/review/** at all). What it does is make the DEFAULT for
# the next artefact "outside the resolver's domain" instead of "inside it, if
# nobody remembers". A card that genuinely needs one tracked force-adds it,
# which is a visible act; tests/test_check_ref_resolution.py's
# `test_no_new_artefact_file_is_force_added_into_the_resolver_domain` holds the
# residue those force-adds have already left.
#
# Scoped by extension rather than by directory, deliberately: the `.md` records
# under meta/review/ and meta/profiling/ are already outside the resolver's
# domain (the `*.md` exclusion) and are read by the suite, and the `.py` tools
# under meta/profiling/ are code that tests/test_guard_integrity.py's
# GUARDED_DIRECTORIES is answerable for -- ignoring those by directory would
# quietly move a future tool outside that guard.
meta/review/*.yml
meta/profiling/*.txt
scratchpad/
